Ask Razer keyboards for their layout with two argument bytes

OpenRGB sends the keyboard-info query (class 0x00, command 0x86) with a
data size of 0, while OpenRazer sends the same query with a data size of
2. The bridge accepts each command only with the sizes in the device's
command list, which is built from what OpenRazer sends, so OpenRGB's
query would be refused before it reaches the keyboard. The two extra
bytes are zero. Whether the keyboard itself cares about the size hasn't
been checked; the command list does.

--- a/Controllers/RazerController/RazerController/RazerController.cpp
+++ b/Controllers/RazerController/RazerController/RazerController.cpp
@@ -1400,7 +1400,7 @@
 
 void RazerController::razer_get_keyboard_info(unsigned char* layout, unsigned char* variant)
 {
-    struct razer_report report              = razer_create_report(0x00, RAZER_COMMAND_ID_GET_KEYBOARD_INFO, 0x00);
+    struct razer_report report              = razer_create_report(0x00, RAZER_COMMAND_ID_GET_KEYBOARD_INFO, 0x02);
     struct razer_report response_report     = razer_create_response();
 
     std::this_thread::sleep_for(1ms);
